      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are applying a focused review fix to the storage module's QueryCatalog (Task 7 already implemented in `src/server/storage/queries.py`).\n\n## The finding (Important)\nIn `QueryCatalog.load` (`src/server/storage/queries.py`), after `data = yaml.safe_load(...) or {}`, the code calls `data.items()`. If a query YAML file's top level is NOT a mapping (e.g. a list `- select 1`, or a scalar/string), `yaml.safe_load` succeeds (no YAMLError) but `data.items()` then raises an unhandled `AttributeError`. The module's contract is that config problems surface as `QueryConfigError`.\n\n## Fix required\n1. In `src/server/storage/queries.py`, right after the YAML is loaded (and the `or {}`), add a guard: if `data` is not a `dict`, raise `QueryConfigError(f\"{f}: expected a mapping of name -> statement, got {type(data).__name__}\")`. Keep the existing YAMLError handling.\n2. While there, make the `get()` method's re-raised `KeyError` use `from None` (so the traceback doesn't show the redundant internal-dict lookup chain) — a one-word change; only do this if `get()` currently re-raises a `KeyError` inside an `except KeyError` block.\n3. Add a test to `tests/server/storage/test_queries.py`: `test_non_mapping_yaml_rejected` — write a yaml file whose top level is a list (e.g. `\"- select 1\\n\"`), and assert `QueryCatalog.load(tmp_path)` raises `QueryConfigError`.\n\nDo NOT change anything else. Follow the existing code style.\n\n## Verify and commit\nRun `pytest tests/server/storage/test_queries.py -v` — all tests (existing 4 + your new one) must pass with pristine output. Then commit with message: `fix(storage): QueryCatalog rejects non-mapping YAML with QueryConfigError`.\n\n## Report\nAPPEND your fix report to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-7-report.md` under a \"## Fix round\" heading: what you changed, the exact test command run, and its full output. Then reply with ONLY: Status (DONE/BLOCKED), commit SHA + subject, the test command + one-line result, and the report path. Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`.",
